{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792889904,"nonce":"ZNNrO/FFns+MYTVEgdV8lRbFBNY=","title":"The live heap is larger than Ash's for the same Haxe program","message":"The ChimpMonk editor's memory probe, with `hl.Gc.major()` twice at each stage,\nreports the live Haxe heap at \"every panel open\" as 218 MB under caribou against\n157 MB under Ash, and 71 MB against 53 MB once every panel is closed. Same\nprogram, same collector design: the difference is what each heap's mark keeps.\n\nThe likely cause is marking that is still conservative where Ash's is precise\nnow:\n- e53ebf70: scan a class instance by its layout, and keep scalar boxes out of\n  the scan. Caribou scans a Typed allocation's every word, and a test pins that\n  a bare hl_type stays conservative, so a stale integer or float that looks\n  like a heap address keeps an object, and what it reaches, alive.\n- 2963f365: skip a large span's interior blocks whole, and keep class tables\n  out of the scan.\n\nDoing this in caribou needs a decision on where the layout knowledge lives:\nthe core is runtime-agnostic and reads layouts only through descriptors and\nhooks, so Ash's instance layout belongs in caribou-ash's descriptor, not in\nthe core's marker.\n\nTools to attribute the difference, also not yet in caribou's heap:\n- 9f0c9e26, f0c7225f: typed heap census in the memory dump, with pages that\n  hold a live line.\n- 5c05c82c, 2982a4cb, 5ebb9078, d3140d4a, 8e57b89c, 1a7d71cb: ASH_GC_DEBUG_ROOTS\n  retention chains (what each root keeps alive and why) and ASH_GC_VERIFY_HEAP.\n\nOther Ash GC changes since the late-September copy, smaller:\n- 67a5f08f: a fiber switch records its stack without the GC lock.\n- e3dd6790: finalizer queue and completion counts on demand.\n- 10ffb264: where a thread a slow world stop waits on is running.\n- e62ce535: clear a block's object marks through as_chunks_mut.\n\nNot applicable (caribou's heap has no minors or adaptive growth): the card\nbarrier (88c0c7ba, ded1b089, f7ceb0c9, 10af36db), 8eae2b15, b0a5df76,\nebbd5e3b.","files":null}]}